  <static seed="850" source="Library/FortLewis/Calc3/19-2-Flux-integrals/HGM4-19-2-05-Flux-integrals.pg">
    <statement><p>Set up a double integral for calculating the flux of 
<m>\vec{F} = 2 x \vec{i} + y \vec{j} + z \vec{k}</m>
through the part of the surface 
<m>z = -4 x - 2 y + 4</m> above the triangle
in the xy-plane with vertices <m>(0,0)</m>, 
<m>(0,3)</m>, and <m>(3,0)</m>, oriented 
upward.</p>
<p><em>Instructions:</em>
Please enter the integrand in the first answer box. 
Depending on the order of integration you choose,  
enter <em>dx</em> and <em>dy</em> 
in either order into the second and third answer boxes 
with only one <em>dx</em> or 
<em>dy</em> in each box.  Then, enter the limits of 
integration and evaluate the integral to find the flux.</p>
<p>Flux = 
<m>\displaystyle \int_A^B \!\! \int_C^D</m> 
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<fillin characters="5" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_1"/>
<fillin characters="5" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_2"/></p>
<p>A = <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_3"/></p>
<p>B = <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_4"/></p>
<p>C = <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_5"/></p>
<p>D = <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_6"/></p>
<p>Flux = 
<m>\displaystyle \iint\limits_S \vec{F} \cdot d\vec{A}</m> =
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4x+4;\,dx;\,dy;\,0;\,3;\,0;\,3-\frac{3}{3}y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>36</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
